        "body":  "Test results on real 3FS, as offered in #62389.\n\n**Setup:** vLLM v0.32.0 with the two changed files of this PR at `ed8a5db` (the PR base is identical to v0.32.0 for these files), plus the one-line metadata URL fix from #62465 (without it each instance talks to a localhost metadata server). Llama-3.1-70B-Instruct, TP4, block size 64. Two instances on two H100 hosts (pod A writes, pod B reads), one shared metadata server (this PR\u0027s file, default lease TTL 120 s), 3FS over FUSE with USRBIO. Small pool on purpose: `hf3fs_file_size` 2 GiB per rank = 409 pages per rank. Needle prompts of about 1,850 tokens with one known answer each; flood prompts of 3,256 tokens (50 new keys each).\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Before the pool is full | B loaded A\u0027s prompts from 3FS (1,792 of 1,850 tokens), answers correct |\n| Sequential flood past the pool (12 prompts) | each prompt evicted exactly 50 keys; free pages stayed 0 on all 4 ranks; B loaded the 3 newest prompts from 3FS (3,200 tokens each) |\n| Concurrent flood (12 prompts, 8 at a time) | B loaded the 3 newest prompts from 3FS (3,200 tokens each) |\n| New prompts after the pool is full | 4 of 4 stored and loaded by B from 3FS (1,792-1,856 tokens), answers correct |\n| Old prompts | stored before the flood: evicted (0 tokens from 3FS on B), answers correct (recomputed) |\n| Lease protects keys | I held a lease with `POST /keys/acquire` on all 4 ranks for one prompt\u0027s 29 keys and never released it (a stalled reader), then flooded: an unleased control prompt had 0 of 29 keys left, the leased prompt 29 of 29; B loaded the leased prompt from 3FS (1,792 tokens), answer correct |\n| Expired lease | 134 s after the acquire, the next flood evicted the leased prompt (0 of 29 keys), `leased` count 0 |\n| Errors | 0 failed saves and 0 failed loads in the vLLM KV transfer metrics on both instances; 0 wrong answers in 28 needle checks |\n\nTwo observations:\n\n1. The lease deadline is the latest deadline of all leases on a key. B read the leased prompt about 10 s after my acquire, so at 125 s 28 of the 29 keys still counted as leased, and they were evicted at 134 s. So a lease that is never released lasts until no reader has touched the key for one TTL. I think that is fine; it may be worth a line in the docs.\n2. Seen once and not reproduced: 15 s after a larger concurrent flood (60 prompts, 8 at a time, about 5 x the pool), B found none of the 3 newest prompts, and free pages were 100 on rank 0 and 50 on ranks 1-3. The 12-prompt floods above did not show it. Saves may still have been in progress; I did not prove the cause.\n\nNot covered: a real reader process killed in the middle of a read (I simulated the stalled reader with `/keys/acquire`), and throughput impact.",
