        "updated_at":  "2026-10-21T03:50:30Z",
        "body":  "Thanks for the test and the docstring. On (2), our saved logs answer it: it was our test timing, not the PR.\n\n- The writer\u0027s last 8 flood requests (they include the 3 newest prompts) were scheduled at 12:24:19-21 UTC. Their saves finished at 12:24:41-46 on all 4 ranks, 21-25 s later. During the flood the save queue fell behind the prefill.\n- The reader checked the 3 newest prompts at 12:24:37-39 (15 s after the flood returned), while those saves were still queued. The reader\u0027s scheduler logged `0 matched (0 blocks)` for them, so the miss was at the scheduler (keys not complete yet), not in the worker.\n- No save failed: `Num save task failed=0` in every writer metrics line of that window (12:24:15, :25, :35, :45), and no `Page allocation failed` or other error line on the writer.\n- The metadata server logged `Evicted key` lines until 12:24:48, which matches the late saves.\n\nSo no debug line is needed for this, and c9b2b40 as is is fine for us. In a next run we will wait until the writer\u0027s save queue is empty before we check.\n\nOne side fact from the same window: the reader computed those 3 prompts and saved them itself at 12:24:38-40, while the writer\u0027s saves of the same prompts were still queued (they completed later). We saw no errors from this double write; we did not check which copy the metadata server kept.",
