        "updated_at":  "2026-10-21T04:45:24Z",
        "body":  "Thanks - the log timeline closes it. \"Scheduler logged 0 matched blocks while the saves were still queued, no save failures, and `Evicted key` kept appearing until 12:24:48\" is exactly the case the design skips: a key that is not complete yet is never an eviction candidate, so the reader sees \"not present\" rather than \"evicted\". Nothing to add on our side, and c9b2b40 stays as is; no debug line.\n\nOn the side fact (reader computing and saving the same three prompts while the writer\u0027s saves were queued): the metadata server has no writer lease, so what happened is the documented cache-hit path, not a bug. `allocate_pages_for_keys` returns the existing page for a complete key (`cached_pages`), so the second writer gets the same page and writes into it instead of allocating a new one - which is why you saw no leaked page, no allocation failure and no error. `confirm_write_for_keys` is idempotent per (key, rank), so the second confirmation just re-records the same page.\n\nWhat that does not give you is serialization: two writers can have those bytes in flight at the same time. For the same key the KV content should be identical (the key hashes model, tokens and block), so the outcome should be correct even if the writes interleave, but I cannot claim protection against a real content mismatch. If that ever shows up, the fix is a write lease like the read lease - deliberately out of scope here so the diff stays at one mechanism.\n\nI updated the PR description-level notes in my own record; nothing in the code changed. Thanks again for spending two H100s on this - the leased-key and expired-lease rows are the ones I could not produce here.\n",
        "author_association":  "NONE",
